      ],
      "source": "https://arklasdahistory.org/a-brief-history-of-williford-arkansas/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The railroad arrived on October 1, 1833, sparking business growth and transforming the town into a regional hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.usacitiesonline.com/arcountywilliford.htm"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Nestled in the Ozark foothills, Williford lies along the Spring River, providing scenic views of the surrounding hills.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.usacitiesonline.com/arcountywilliford.htm"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Williford’s first school opened in a church building, with a dedicated schoolhouse following in 1890.",
